    <item>
      <title>Hugo Markdown Styling &amp; Formatting Guide</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/posts/markdown-styling-and-syntax-guide/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Mar 2026 12:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Blanket Statement Team</dc:creator>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">//localhost:1313/posts/markdown-styling-and-syntax-guide/</guid>
      <description>A comprehensive showcase of typography, code highlighting, tables, quotes, and media formatting available in this Hugo blog starter.</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This starter template includes rich formatting support for technical writing, tutorial posts, and personal blogging. Below is a preview of the typography and components.</p>
<h2 id="headings--typography">Headings &amp; Typography</h2>
<p>Here is standard body text with <strong>bold text</strong>, <em>italic text</em>, and <code>inline code</code>.</p>
<h3 id="subheading-level-3">Subheading Level 3</h3>
<p>Paragraph text flows smoothly with readable line heights and carefully tuned margins matching the Blanket Statement visual identity.</p>
<h4 id="subheading-level-4">Subheading Level 4</h4>
<p>Lists are formatted with clean spacing:</p>
<ul>
<li>First bullet point with helpful context</li>
<li>Second bullet point with <a href="/">a link to home</a></li>
<li>Third bullet point with embedded sub-items:
<ul>
<li>Sub-item A</li>
<li>Sub-item B</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="blockquotes">Blockquotes</h2>
<blockquote>
<p>&ldquo;Productive fidgeting transforms passive listening into active, engaged presence while building something beautiful for others.&rdquo;</p>
</blockquote>
<h2 id="code-syntax-highlighting">Code Syntax Highlighting</h2>
<p>Hugo&rsquo;s built-in Chroma syntax engine formats code with high contrast:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"><code class="language-python" data-lang="python"><span style="display:flex;"><span><span style="color:#66d9ef">def</span> <span style="color:#a6e22e">knit_square</span>(stitches<span style="color:#f92672">=</span><span style="color:#ae81ff">30</span>, rows<span style="color:#f92672">=</span><span style="color:#ae81ff">48</span>):
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>    <span style="color:#e6db74">&#34;&#34;&#34;Simulate knitting a 7x9 inch square.&#34;&#34;&#34;</span>
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>    fabric <span style="color:#f92672">=</span> []
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>    <span style="color:#66d9ef">for</span> r <span style="color:#f92672">in</span> range(rows):
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>        fabric<span style="color:#f92672">.</span>append([<span style="color:#e6db74">&#34;knit&#34;</span> <span style="color:#66d9ef">for</span> _ <span style="color:#f92672">in</span> range(stitches)])
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>    print(<span style="color:#e6db74">f</span><span style="color:#e6db74">&#34;Finished square with </span><span style="color:#e6db74">{</span>rows<span style="color:#e6db74">}</span><span style="color:#e6db74"> rows of </span><span style="color:#e6db74">{</span>stitches<span style="color:#e6db74">}</span><span style="color:#e6db74"> stitches!&#34;</span>)
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>    <span style="color:#66d9ef">return</span> fabric
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span><span style="color:#66d9ef">if</span> __name__ <span style="color:#f92672">==</span> <span style="color:#e6db74">&#34;__main__&#34;</span>:
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>    knit_square()
</span></span></code></pre></div><p>And in Go / Hugo template syntax:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"><code class="language-go" data-lang="go"><span style="display:flex;"><span>{{ <span style="color:#66d9ef">range</span> <span style="color:#a6e22e">where</span> .<span style="color:#a6e22e">Site</span>.<span style="color:#a6e22e">RegularPages</span> <span style="color:#e6db74">&#34;Section&#34;</span> <span style="color:#e6db74">&#34;posts&#34;</span> }}
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>  &lt;<span style="color:#a6e22e">article</span>&gt;
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>    &lt;<span style="color:#a6e22e">h2</span>&gt;{{ .<span style="color:#a6e22e">Title</span> }}&lt;<span style="color:#f92672">/</span><span style="color:#a6e22e">h2</span>&gt;
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>    &lt;<span style="color:#a6e22e">p</span>&gt;{{ .<span style="color:#a6e22e">Summary</span> }}&lt;<span style="color:#f92672">/</span><span style="color:#a6e22e">p</span>&gt;
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>  &lt;<span style="color:#f92672">/</span><span style="color:#a6e22e">article</span>&gt;
</span></span><span style="display:flex;"><span>{{ <span style="color:#a6e22e">end</span> }}
</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="tables">Tables</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
      <tr>
          <th style="text-align: left">Metric</th>
          <th style="text-align: left">Target</th>
          <th style="text-align: left">Notes</th>
      </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
      <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left"><strong>Block Width</strong></td>
          <td style="text-align: left">7 inches</td>
          <td style="text-align: left">Standard size</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left"><strong>Block Length</strong></td>
          <td style="text-align: left">9 inches</td>
          <td style="text-align: left">Direction doesn&rsquo;t matter</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left"><strong>Yarn Weight</strong></td>
          <td style="text-align: left">Worsted (#4)</td>
          <td style="text-align: left">Washable acrylic or wool blend</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left"><strong>Needle Size</strong></td>
          <td style="text-align: left">US 8 (5.0mm)</td>
          <td style="text-align: left">Provides flexible drape</td>
      </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<h2 id="image-embeds">Image Embeds</h2>
<p>Images are automatically responsive with rounded corners and subtle shadows:</p>
<p><img src="/img/balls-of-yarn.jpg" alt="Knitting with colorful yarn"></p>
<p>Enjoy writing your posts with Hugo!</p>
]]></content:encoded>
